From 7044757349c66076c370330f6172010cc7ecc9f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:54:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mempool: check consistency in existing topological order

The entry-id index already orders every parent before its children. Use it to check and apply scratch UTXOs in one pass instead of retrying children encountered through the hashed TxId index. Direct-parent ordering assertions prove the redundant transitive ancestor ordering check by induction, avoiding a full ancestor walk for each entry.

Preserve graph, coin, pointer, fee, size and cached-memory assertions. Add a 512-node repeated-parent-input chain fixture, hashed-index ordering check and recursive prefix/removal checks. This changes only the optional whole-pool diagnostic, not admission policy or block selection; per-insertion whole-pool checking still has aggregate quadratic cost.
---
 src/test/mempool_tests.cpp | 46 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/txmempool.cpp          | 35 +++++------------------------
 2 files changed, 51 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/test/mempool_tests.cpp b/src/test/mempool_tests.cpp
index 72b8102ce..fddd96ff7 100644
--- a/src/test/mempool_tests.cpp
+++ b/src/test/mempool_tests.cpp
@@ -5,6 +5,9 @@
 
 #include <txmempool.h>
 
